  "description": "<p>Given two integer arrays <code>nums1</code> and <code>nums2</code>, return <em>an array of their <span class=\"cursor-pointer relative text-dark-blue-s text-sm\" data-keyword=\"array-intersection\"><button aria-controls=\"radix-_r_1m_\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\" type=\"button\">intersection</button></span></em>. Each element in the result must be <strong>unique</strong> and you may return the result in <strong>any order</strong>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums1 = [1,2,2,1], nums2 = [2,2]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [2]\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums1 = [4,9,5], nums2 = [9,4,9,8,4]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [9,4]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> [4,9] is also accepted.\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>1 &lt;= nums1.length, nums2.length &lt;= 1000</code></li> <li><code>0 &lt;= nums1[i], nums2[i] &lt;= 1000</code></li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
